This package contains no FFmpeg binary. On first use it downloads, from the GitHub Release named
in src/manifest.ts (or from MOTIO_FFMPEG_BASE_URL), an archive with FFmpeg and ffprobe built by
the scripts in tools/ffmpeg-build/ of the Motio repository, and checks it against the SHA-256
digest in src/manifest.ts.

Those binaries are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later, because
they include x264 and x265 (GPL-2.0-or-later) and are configured with --enable-gpl and
--enable-version3 (Mbed TLS). They statically link:

- FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), LGPL-2.1-or-later, GPL as configured
- x264 (https://www.videolan.org/developers/x264.html), GPL-2.0-or-later
- x265 (https://www.x265.org), GPL-2.0-or-later
- SVT-AV1 (https://gitlab.com/AOMediaCodec/SVT-AV1), BSD-3-Clause-Clear and the Alliance for
  Open Media Patent License 1.0
- libvpx (https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libvpx), BSD-3-Clause and the WebM patent grant
- dav1d (https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d), BSD-2-Clause
- Opus (https://opus-codec.org), BSD-3-Clause
- LAME (https://lame.sourceforge.io), LGPL-2.0-or-later
- Mbed TLS (https://www.trustedfirmware.org/projects/mbed-tls/), Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later
- Linux builds only: zlib (https://zlib.net), zlib licence; musl libc (https://musl.libc.org), MIT

Every archive contains LICENSE.md, the licence text of each library in licenses/, and
BUILDINFO.json, which lists each source with its SHA-256 and the configure flags. The release
that publishes the archives also publishes the exact source tarballs, their digests and the
build scripts.
